    <!-- CONTENT -->
    <main class="pp-main">
      <h1 class="pp-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="pp-updated">Last updated: September 2026</p>

      <p class="pp-lead">Droparabia is committed to protecting your personal information. This Privacy Policy explains what data we collect, how we use it, and how we keep it safe when you visit droparabia.com or any of its pages, watch our free tutorial, complete our survey, or book a call with our team.</p>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2 class="pp-heading">1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <ul class="pp-list">
          <li><strong>Personal data</strong> you give us: your name, email address, and WhatsApp number.</li>
          <li><strong>Survey responses</strong>: your answers to our qualification questions, including your business goals and available budget.</li>
          <li><strong>Booking details</strong>: information you provide when scheduling a call through Calendly.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage data</strong>: pages visited, time spent, how much of our tutorial you watched, links clicked, and where you are in our sign-up journey.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2 class="pp-heading">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul class="pp-list">
          <li>To give you access to our tutorial, platform, and team</li>
          <li>To contact you about your booking, account, follow-ups, and offers</li>
          <li>To understand whether our programs are a good fit for you</li>
          <li>To improve our content, offers, and user experience</li>
          <li>To measure and improve the performance of our advertising</li>
          <li>For legal compliance and security</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2 class="pp-heading">3. Cookies and Tracking</h2>
        <p class="pp-text">We use cookies and similar technologies, including Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager, and the Meta Pixel, to understand how visitors use our site, measure the performance of our ads, and show relevant ads on Facebook and Instagram.</p>
        <p class="pp-text">The Meta Pixel may collect information such as your IP address, browser details, pages visited, and actions taken on our site. Where you provide your email or phone number, it may be shared with Meta in hashed (encrypted) form to match your visit with your Meta account for advertising measurement.</p>
        <p class="pp-text">You can control ad personalization through your Facebook and Instagram ad settings, and block cookies through your browser settings.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2 class="pp-heading">4. Data Sharing</h2>
        <p class="pp-text">We do not sell or rent your personal data. We share data only with trusted third-party services when necessary to operate our platform and marketing:</p>
        <ul class="pp-list">
          <li><strong>Brevo</strong> — email and SMS communication</li>
          <li><strong>Google</strong> (Analytics, Tag Manager, Sheets) — analytics and lead management</li>
          <li><strong>Calendly</strong> — call scheduling</li>
          <li><strong>Meta Platforms</strong> — advertising measurement and optimization</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2 class="pp-heading">5. Data Security</h2>
        <p class="pp-text">We use secure platforms and encryption to protect your data. No system is 100% secure, but we take reasonable steps to safeguard your information.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2 class="pp-heading">6. Data Retention</h2>
        <p class="pp-text">We keep your information for as long as needed to provide our services and follow up with you, or until you ask us to delete it.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2 class="pp-heading">7. Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="pp-text">You can request to access, correct, or delete your personal data at any time, or ask to stop receiving our messages. Reach out to us on Instagram at <a href="https://www.instagram.com/mjbusinessofficial" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="pp-link">@mjbusinessofficial</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2 class="pp-heading">8. Policy Updates</h2>
        <p class="pp-text">We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The most recent version will always be posted on this page, with the date it was last updated.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2 class="pp-heading">9. Meta Advertising Measurement</h2>
        <p class="pp-text">We use the Meta Pixel to measure how our advertising performs, and we share conversion data with Meta so we can see which ads lead to sign-ups and bookings.</p>
        <p class="pp-text">Your email address and phone number are cryptographically hashed before they are transmitted, so Meta does not receive them in plain text.</p>
        <p class="pp-text">When you arrive from a Meta ad, the link carries a click identifier. We store it in your browser so that a sign-up or booking you make on a later page can be credited to the ad that brought you here.</p>
        <p class="pp-text">We do not ourselves collect or store your IP address or any device fingerprint. As with any third-party script, Meta receives standard technical information when its pixel loads, including your IP address and browser user agent.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="pp-section">
        <h2 class="pp-heading">Contact</h2>
        <p class="pp-text">If you have any questions about this policy, message us on Instagram at <a href="https://www.instagram.com/mjbusinessofficial" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="pp-link">@mjbusinessofficial</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </main>

